ype": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn11le02ob09re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 0}], "id": 0}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"_data": [], "id": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn11le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn11le02ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn11le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn11le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "The practice of mindful meditation involves becoming aware of your \u201cstream of consciousness\u201d. Mindfulness has been shown to have multiple health benefits, specifically for its proven ability to decrease rumination.\n<br/>\nJoseph Hay came across mindfulness after moving to British Columbia. \u201cI was doing a lot of yoga, but I found that my instructors focused exclusively on the physical, almost as if it were just a workout,\u201d he says. \u201cThat's when I switched to mindful meditation, and I'm so much happier for having discovered it. Since adopting mindfulness, I've noticed a dramatic improvement in my overall well-being.\u201d"}, {"time": "31000", "image": "engenn11le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "With so many people living fast-paced lives, it's no wonder there's an increasing need to slow down and take stock of one's thoughts and feelings. Joseph now conducts mindfulness seminars for local businesses.\n<br/>\n\u201cIf you're in a corporate environment, you spend all of your time worrying about projects and deadlines,\u201d he explains. \u201cThe goal of my sessions is to get people to slow down and get in touch with their own thoughts.\u201d\n<br/>\nAfter speaking with several of his corporate clients during his most recent retreat in Vancouver, it's easy to see why his seminars are completely booked up through the end of the year. The response was almost unanimously positive. Many of them even said that it was a life-altering experience, and that they would strongly advise their colleagues to attend. They promised they would find the time to meditate each day, even with their busy work schedules."}, {"time": "74000", "image": "engenn11le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Although the overwhelming majority were satisfied, one distraught employee ended up arriving four hours late and missing the entire session. He remembered writing the event down in his agenda, but he says that he was so busy thinking about his big presentation,  he didn't have time to double-check the schedule.\n<br/>\nHe apologized for missing the seminar. \u201cI guess mindfulness means paying attention to what's going on in the outside world, not just what's going on in my head,\u201d he said. \u201cAfter all, you can't be mindful if your mind is too full.\u201d"}]}}], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "id": 0}]}